Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:21:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ce_main_app: add, make and delete files in hard disk images
 (Look inside)

POST /api/v1/settings/hddimage/inspectwrite?op=put&path=&part=&dir=&name=
[&overwrite=1] with the file as the body (application/octet-stream, at
most 64 MB), op=mkdir (&dir=&name=), op=rm (&file=: a file, or a folder
with what's in it). Done by /usr/sbin/ce-hdinspect: only images the ST has
on no ID, opened writable for that one change; FAT (GEMDOS) names become
8.3 in capitals. The body goes straight to the tool's stdin (no copy); a
name already there answers 409 with "exists".

Attaching an image while a change is written into it is refused
(/run/ce-hdinspect/writing).
---
 .../api/resource/settingsresource.cpp         | 124 +++++++++++++++++-
 .../webserver/api/resource/settingsresource.h |   4 +-
 2 files changed, 123 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

